---
import { site } from '@/config/site';
---

<section id="ways" class="wrap ways">
  <div class="section-head">
    <h2 class="h2" style="max-width:18ch">
      One engine. Drive it from the app, the terminal or an assistant.
    </h2>
    <p class="lede">
      A background engine runs the radio and keeps listening when the window is closed. The Mac app,
      the <span class="mono ley">ley</span> command and MCP clients all talk to it, so a squelch
      change in the terminal shows up in the window, and an assistant can scan a band while you
      listen.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="cards">
    <div class="card">
      <div class="card-head">
        <span class="label mono">The app</span>
        <span class="desc">Waterfall, bands, inspector and Library. For listening.</span>
      </div>
      <div class="mini" aria-hidden="true">
        <div class="mini-bar">
          <span></span>
          <span></span>
          <span></span>
        </div>
        <div class="mini-main">
          <div class="mini-side">
            <span style="width:80%;background:var(--line-4)"></span>
            <span style="width:65%"></span>
            <span style="width:72%"></span>
            <span style="width:58%"></span>
          </div>
          <canvas data-waterfall-mini width="240" height="140"></canvas>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="card">
      <div class="card-head">
        <span class="label mono">The terminal</span>
        <span class="desc">
          <span class="mono code">ley</span> for scripts, cron jobs and SSH. Every command has{' '}
          <span class="mono code">--json</span>.
        </span>
      </div>
      <pre class="term shell"><span class="cmd">$ ley tune 146.52</span>
using NFM: 2 m amateur band default
Squelch auto → -80 dBFS
<span class="hi">146.520 MHz NFM  -39 dBFS  <span class="teal">audio</span></span>

<span class="cmd">$ ley set squelch -45</span>
squelch -80 → -45 dBFS</pre>
    </div>

    <div class="card">
      <div class="card-head">
        <span class="label mono">An assistant</span>
        <span class="desc">
          <span class="mono code">ley mcp</span> gives an AI assistant the same tools, over MCP.
        </span>
      </div>
      <div class="chat">
        <div class="bubble me">Scan 2 m and tell me what’s active.</div>
        <div class="tool mono">scan 144M..148M</div>
        <div class="bubble them">
          Three carriers. 146.520 (calling) and 145.230 were up for the whole sweep; 146.940 showed
          once.
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <a href={site.links.docs} class="mono docs">
    Read the docs for ley and MCP →
  </a>
</section>

<style>
  .ways {
    padding-top: 160px;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 44px;
  }

  .ley {
    font-size: 14px;
    color: var(--text-2);
  }

  .cards {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(100%, 250px), 1fr));
    gap: 16px;
  }

  .card {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    border: 1px solid var(--line-3);
    border-radius: 11px;
    overflow: hidden;
    background: var(--surface);
  }

  .card-head {
    padding: 20px 22px 16px;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 6px;
  }

  .label {
    font-size: 11px;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--accent);
  }

  .desc {
    font-size: 15px;
    line-height: 1.5;
    color: var(--text-2);
    text-wrap: pretty;
  }

  .code {
    font-size: 13px;
  }

  .mini {
    flex: 1;
    min-height: 170px;
    margin: 0 22px 22px;
    border: 1px solid var(--line-2);
    border-radius: 8px;
    overflow: hidden;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    background: var(--bg);
  }

  .mini-bar {
    height: 22px;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 5px;
    padding: 0 9px;
    background: var(--surface-2);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line-2);
  }

  .mini-bar span {
    width: 7px;
    height: 7px;
    border-radius: 50%;
  }

  .mini-bar span:nth-child(1) {
    background: #ff5f57;
  }

  .mini-bar span:nth-child(2) {
    background: #febc2e;
  }

  .mini-bar span:nth-child(3) {
    background: #28c840;
  }

  .mini-main {
    flex: 1;
    display: flex;
    min-height: 0;
  }

  .mini-side {
    width: 26%;
    background: var(--surface);
    border-right: 1px solid var(--line-2);
    padding: 8px 6px;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 5px;
  }

  .mini-side span {
    height: 5px;
    border-radius: 2px;
    background: var(--surface-hi);
  }

  .mini canvas {
    display: block;
    flex: 1;
    min-width: 0;
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
  }

  .shell {
    flex: 1;
    margin: 0 22px 22px;
    border: 1px solid var(--line-2);
    border-radius: 8px;
    background: var(--bg-deep);
    padding: 14px;
    font-size: 11px;
    line-height: 1.8;
  }

  .chat {
    flex: 1;
    margin: 0 22px 22px;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 9px;
    font-size: 13px;
    line-height: 1.5;
    font-family: var(--font-mac);
  }

  .bubble {
    padding: 9px 12px;
    text-wrap: pretty;
  }

  .me {
    align-self: flex-end;
    max-width: 86%;
    border-radius: 12px 12px 3px;
    background: var(--surface-sel);
    color: var(--text-bright);
  }

  .them {
    align-self: flex-start;
    max-width: 92%;
    border-radius: 12px 12px 12px 3px;
    background: var(--surface-3);
    color: var(--text-2);
  }

  .tool {
    align-self: flex-start;
    padding: 5px 9px;
    border-radius: 6px;
    border: 1px solid var(--teal-deep);
    font-size: 10.5px;
    color: var(--teal);
  }

  .docs {
    align-self: flex-start;
    font-size: 12px;
  }
</style>
